    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is proud to present 119 Georgian Village, an exceptional detached five-bedroom family residence that has been comprehensively renovated and beautifully extended to an impressive c. 385 sq. m. / 4,144 sq. ft. Occupying a prime corner setting, this distinguished home enjoys a private south-west facing rear garden, perfectly positioned to capture sunlight throughout the day. Ideally located within walking distance of both the Phoenix Park and the amenities of Castleknock Village, the property offers an enviable combination of space, convenience and lifestyle. Meticulously maintained and thoughtfully designed by its previous current owners, the home has undergone an extensive transformation, seamlessly blending contemporary design with practical family living. Finished to an exacting standard throughout, the result is a luxurious and elegant residence that provides every modern comfort while retaining a warm and welcoming atmosphere. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial turnkey family home in one of Castleknock's most sought-after residential locations.\n\nFrom the moment of arrival, this impressive residence exudes quality and refinement. Elegant granite steps and meticulously crafted granite borders create a striking first impression, setting the tone for the exceptional accommodation that lies within. Upon entering, the magnificent double-height entrance hall immediately conveys a wonderful sense of grandeur, space, and natural light. The welcoming reception hall provides access to three of the home's five superb reception rooms. To the right, a beautifully appointed formal dining room features an elegant marble fireplace and interconnecting double doors leading seamlessly to both the principal drawing room and the impressive sunroom beyond. The main reception room is wonderfully proportioned, centered around a feature marble fireplace and enhanced by a large bay window that floods the room with natural light while creating an ideal setting for both entertaining and everyday living. To the left of the hall, a further substantial reception room offers exceptional versatility. Featuring an elegant marble fireplace, impressive c. 3m ceilings, a large bay window, and oak timber flooring, this space is currently utilised as a private gym but could equally serve as a family room, home office, library, or games room. A connecting door leads to the fifth reception room and rear lobby, where a guest cloakroom/WC is conveniently located. At the heart of the home lies a beautifully fitted kitchen designed with both style and practicality in mind. Featuring a large breakfast island, an extensive range of integrated appliances, and provision for an American-style fridge freezer, this is a space perfectly tailored to modern family living. Double doors open into the spectacular sunroom, an outstanding addition that spans the full width of the property. With its vaulted ceiling, abundant natural light, and uninterrupted views over the rear gardens, this exceptional room provides the perfect setting for relaxed family gatherings and elegant entertaining alike. French doors open directly onto the patio and gardens beyond, seamlessly connecting the indoor and outdoor living spaces.\n\nUpstairs, the property offers five generously proportioned double bedrooms, providing luxurious accommodation for family and guests alike. Four bedrooms benefit from stylish fully tiled en-suite shower rooms, while both the principal suite and second bedroom are enhanced by spacious walk-in wardrobes. A beautifully appointed family bathroom completes this level. From the landing, a staircase leads to a versatile attic room with Velux windows, ideal as a home office, studio, playroom, or private retreat.\n\nExternally, the property continues to impress. A mature laurel hedge provides both privacy and elegance along the front boundary, opening onto a generous granite-edged driveway with ample off-street parking for up to four vehicles. Gated side access leads to the rear gardens, where a substantial block-built shed with power supply offers excellent storage or workshop potential. The private rear garden enjoys a highly desirable southerly orientation and is primarily laid in lawn, framed by mature specimen trees that provide a wonderful sense of seclusion. An attractive Indian sandstone patio creates a superb outdoor entertaining area, perfectly suited to al fresco dining and summer gatherings in a peaceful and picturesque setting.\n\nGeorgian Village's location needs little introduction, it is superbly positioned between Castleknock Village and the Phoenix Park. Pedestrian access onto both Whites Road and Castleknock Road, virtually at the gates of the Phoenix Park, ensure that both the Village and the Park are just a 5-minute walk. There are excellent National & Secondary Schools within close walking distance. A host of sporting clubs, including Castleknock Tennis Club, Cricket, Polo, Horseback riding, GAA, Rugby and several Golf Clubs are located in the immediate vicinity. Shopping and dining options abound locally. For the commuter, access to the N3, M3 and M50 is particularly convenient. City Centre which is well served by bus and train is 7km, the IFSC is 8km, Four Courts 6 KM, Mater Misericordiae Hospital 6km & Dublin Airport is 16 km, (15/20 minutes' drive). Heuston Train Station and the Luas hub are 5km. All times and distances are approximate.\n\nThis is an unrivalled opportunity to acquire a superb family home and viewing is highly recommended and is by private appointment with Sherry FitzGerald Castleknock."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 7.19m x 3.00m\nDouble height 5m high ceilings create a grand entrance, feature panelled walls and an attractive black & white tiled flooring.\n\nDrawing Room - 8.27m x 4.70m\nLarge drawing room with feature Bay window providing plenty of natural light, marble fireplace with decorative coving and centre rose.\n\nDining Room - 7.20m x 4.32m\nLocated to the right of the hallway, large formal reception room with marble fireplace, decorative coving and centre rose, interconnecting doors with drawing room and rear sunroom.\n\nSunroom - 10.37m x 8.0m\nAn impressive addition to the property is the large openplan sunroom/family room. Feature vaulted 3.3 m high ceilings and French doors lead to the rear garden.\n\nFamily Room - 7.18m x 3.60m\nLocated to the left of the hallway with feature marble fireplace, decorative coving and centre rose.\n\nGym - 6.60m x 4.60m\nCurrently in use as a Gym, this large reception room could be utilised as another family room. Feature 4m high ceilings with recessed lighting and an attractive bay style window to the front. Oak timber flooring.\n\nRear lobby - 4.60m x 3.00m\nWith tiled flooring and door to side passage/rear garden. Tiled flooring.\n\nGuest Cloak Closet/WC - 1.80m x 0.80m\nLocated off the rear lobby, fully tiled and comprises of WC and wash hand basin.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast area - 5.40m x 4.55m\nModern fully fitted kitchen with an excellent range of floor and eye level presses and breakfast island. Full range of integrated appliances including oven hob and extractor fan, dishwasher, washing machine, plumbed for American style fridge/freezer. Tiled flooring and partly tiled walls.\n\nLanding - 11.30m x 0.80m\nGallery style landing with hotpress and airing cupboard.\n\nPrimary Suite - 6.10m x 4.65m\nLarge double bedroom with Bay window, laminate timber flooring.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.90m x 1.40m\nWith fitted fashion rails\n\nEn-Suite - 1.88m x 1.70m\nComprising of shower, wc and wash hand basin, fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 2 - 6.60m x 4.50m\nLarge double bedroom, laminate timber flooring. Shutter blinds. Shutter blinds.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.95m x 1.30m\nWith fitted fashion rails\n\nEn-Suite - 1.88m x 1.71m\nComprises of shower, wc and wash hand basin, fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.0m x 3.70m\nLarge double bedroom, laminate timber flooring. Shutter blinds.\n\nEn-Suite - 1.80m x 1.70m\nComprises of shower, wc and wash hand basin, fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 4 - 5.20m x 3.70m\nLarge double bedroom, laminate timber flooring. Shutter blinds.\n\nEn-Suite - 1.87m x 1.70m\nComprises of shower, wc and wash hand basin, fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 5 - 3.30m x 2.80m\nDouble bedroom, laminate timber flooring. Shutter blinds.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 3.20m x 2.20m\nGood sized family bathroom with bath, shower overhead, wc and wash hand basin. Fully tiled.\n\nInner Landing - 3.30m x 2.0m\nStairs to attic.\n\nAttic Room - 6.60m x 3.50m\nLarge attic room with Velux windows, suitable for a variety of uses. office, gym, children's play area etc. Access doors to eaves storage.\n\n"
      },
